With Australia and Qatar, which had pulled out all the registers with the maintenance of futuristic stadiums, FIFA is pursuing its expansion towards new regions, but these two countries pose a greater risk, because certainty.
Australia, like Japan and South Korea, could suffer from the weakness of television rights (due to the time difference) acquired by European countries, FIFA's sensitive nerve.
