European countries, which are well aware of both this divide and the danger hidden in it, are intensifying the discussions to strengthen the anti-crisis measures that already exist.
The informal consultations between the most directly affected finance ministers and, in a broader sense, with their counterparts to the G20 are progressing well.
And also with regard to the meetings of Eurogroupe and Ecofin early next week.
The ECB is meeting today.
On the plan is the lot of unconventional measures to bolstrace the eurozone countries in the crosshairs of the markets (see below).
As far as the EU Stability Fund is concerned, its Executive Director Klaus Regling has already started his tour of Asia in Singapour on Tuesday to inform investors in the Far East about developments regarding the crisis in Europe.
