Yesterday, an official American representative had confided to Reuters that the United States supported a possible increase in the fund mobilized by the IMF's additional, direct commitment.
Portugal and Spain, the countries in the first place, are preparing to undertake structural reforms, in particular in the field of labour market organisation.
Reforms that are added to the austerity measures, but should show effects in the near future.
Lisbon and Madrid take a different path than Greece and Ireland did.
Both one and the other, at any price, is to avoid having to solicit international assistance before setting up their own budget correctives and deciding on unavoidable structural reforms that in the long run their trust.
European investors, in turn, are talking about the options available to accelerate the normalization process of markets of government bonds.
Axel Weber, who was passing through Paris on 24 November, was the first to come up with the idea that if the €750 mobilised by Europe and the International Monetary Fund would not be enough, the Union would not reluctant to reach into its own pocket again.
Barclays Capital's economists, with regard to the market of European public debit in the foreground, judge that an extension of around €100 billion would suffice, "preferably" in the form of a direct injection of liquidity.
This means exists: the European mechanism of endowed financial stabilisation, which is currently €60 billion.
An advisory board that has all the chances of being studied attentively in European capitals.
Especially when market conditions are worsening.
Snow and freezing ice: 24 departments at alarm level orange
The episodes of snoothing are stilling with traffic difficulties, especially in Brittany’s secondary transport networks, and threaten to impair various economic activities.
Twenty-four departments are now in orange alert due to imminent snow and freezing risk.
The regions Eure-et-Loir, Deux-Sèvres and Vienne have been added to the 20 departments, which are already in alarm stage orange; 18 since Wednesday afternoon and two, the Dordogne and the Gironde, later at night.
According to Météo France, the intense snow showers affect the north of the Gironde as well as the Charentes, it snows slightly on et Ile-de-France.
In the affected departments, blankets of 2 to 5 cm are expected, in some places from 7 to 10 cm, as well as 1 to 3 cm, even up to 5 cm in the Paris region.
Affected are Charente, Charente-Maritime, Côtes d'Armor, Finistère, Gironde, Dordogne, Poitou and the regions Basse-Normandie, Ile-de-France and Limousin.
The sneeries are considerable enough to evoke traffic obstructions and impair certain economic activities, Météo France predicts.
In the Côtes d'Armor region, several regional roads are closed to heavy traffic of over 7.5 tonnes, including Guingamp-Lannion and Saint-Brieuc-Loudéac.
The traffic situation of the secondary traffic networks in Brittany is very difficult, according to the traffic polices who advise against using their own vehicle only in emergencies, and the use of some TER coaches has been canceled throughout the day.
In Picardy, school traffic has been lifted for Thursday.
No specific restrictive measures were envisaged for heavy traffic on Wednesday evening.
The prefecture "urges motorists to the utmost caution on the roads as well as the appropriate adaptation of their driving behaviour."
The Directorate-General for Civil Aviation (DGAC) urged the airlines to cancel on Thursday 25% of their flights departing from Parisian Roissy Airport and 10% of flights departing from Orly due to the anticipated heavy snowfall.
The DGAB advises air passengers to contact their airline.
Gatwick airports in south London, as well as the airport in Edinburgh, Scotland, are closed until Thursday morning.
Métro Grand Paris: first financial sketches
